WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.060
If you look at the indictments of the Russians
who were involved in this influence campaign

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.880
these very clever Russian operatives had been
infiltrating social media in the United States

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.480
in an effort to set people against each other
and also to elect Donald Trump.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:23.580
But when you look at what they actually did,
you will start to see that is a big exaggeration

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.860
that's the thesis!

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.040
Information warfare against the United States.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.740
Whatever platform you look at, the amount
of material that the Russians generated

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.960
was just a tiny tiny fraction of what was
out there.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:47.300
According to the indictment the Russians spent
thousands of dollars on social media ads each month.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.060
Well that's about a millionth of the ad revenue
that Facebook alone receives each month.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.540
It's the same story if you look at YouTube,

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.380
the Russians were responsible for producing
43 hours of political content.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.480
Which may seem like a lot until you realize

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:06.480
that 400 hours of content are uploaded to YouTube every minute.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.420
Most of them have low view counts, less than
3% had more than 5000 views.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:16.040
So clearly this did not amount to much in
the context of advertising online

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.720
and the context of online speech.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.040
Information warfare against the United States.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:26.600
Supposedly these Russian trolls were very
sophisticated about the American political system,

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.920
they knew exactly what they were doing, they
knew how to manipulate American voters.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.700
But if you look at what they actually did,
they look not so professional.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.840
A lot of these posts sound like they are written
by people whose native language is not English.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.960
And you would expect sophisticated operatives
to speak better English

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:45.159
so they could pass themselves off as American.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:49.480
They created some very crude propaganda that
they seemed to think would be effective.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.680
For example, there's an ad on Facebook that
showed Jesus arm wrestling with Satan.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:57.479
Now you may say to yourself 'that seems ridiculous.'

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.640
But perhaps people will fall for that.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.420
In fact, it generated very little interest,
very few clicks, very few viewings.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.680
Information warfare against the United States.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.480
The indictment makes much of pro Trump and
anti Clinton rallies

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.840
that were instigated by Russians.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.140
But it doesn't tell us how many people actually
participated in these rallies

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.110
or whether they came off at all.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:28.000
There's one example of a rally in Texas that
was organized to oppose Sharia law

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.840
and according to the New York Times it attracted
a dozen people.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.180
There was a counter protest that according
to the New York Times

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.060
was also organized by the Russians

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:41.760
and attracted a much larger crowd, that could
be two dozen or three dozen people for all we know.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.760
We know that some people in the real world
responded to the agitation for rallies.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.340
But we don't know whether this really amounted
to a significant percentage of voters.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:55.519
Information warfare against the United States.

00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:57.550
Nor do we know any of this advertising,

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:01.580
even the ad that got more attention than the
one with Jesus arm wrestling Satan,

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.110
whether they actually changed anybody's mind,
or energized them in any way,

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:09.080
or got them to behave in any way different
from how they would have behaved otherwise.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.940
You know, pro Trump people might turn out
for a pro Trump rally.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.360
Anti Clinton people might come out for an
anti Clinton rally.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.140
But the fact that they show up does not necessarily
change the outcome of the election

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:23.560
or make the United States a more acrimonious,
you know, society let alone sow chaos.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.519
Information warfare against the United States.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:32.360
And the reason that this sort of hysterical
response is rather alarming

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.180
is that at bottom we're talking about speech.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.360
If you look at the actual content of these
ads, these tweets,

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:43.750
it's not qualitatively different from all
the, you know, home grown-

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.870
all the home grown crap you can routinely
see online.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:51.360
this is essentially the same, I mean, doesn't
mean it's good, doesn't mean it's substantive,

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.780
doesn't even mean it's accurate.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.800
Some of the arguments might have held some
water, some of them were completely ridiculous.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.040
That's true of American political discourse
in general.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.440
It's simply the fact that these people were
born in another country

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.380
that somehow makes this more alarming than
it would otherwise be.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.799
I mean if there is a problem with American
democracy

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:14.400
in the sense that people are easily swayed
by emotion,

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.410
this is not a problem that the Russians created,

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.780
this is a problem that is much broader than
that.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:25.900
And to try and blame, you know, divisions
within the American political culture on the Russians

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.780
seems completely absurd to me.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.360
It's much easier, you know, to blame foreign
invaders for these problems

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.380
but the truth is that if voters are making
decisions for stupid reasons

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.360
that is not the Russians' fault.

